{"id":"2fab6323-b60a-52da-8946-a8eeaee08748","protocol_id":"0c5ca4a7-0e1f-4a52-9a0b-5c1c6c1f0a31","display_name":"4–6 Breathing","item_type":"activity","kind":"action","category":"do","subtype":"wellness","group_name":"Breathwork and nervous-system exercises","scheduled_time":"07:18:00","duration_minutes":3,"day_number":7,"sort_order":50,"recurrence_type":"daily","recurrence_interval_unit":"day","catalog_activity_id":"activity_oscar_4_6_breathing","notes":"Dose: No verified count; a few minutes is typical.\n1. Sit upright with relaxed shoulders.\n2. Breathe in through the nose for 4 seconds.\n3. Breathe out slowly for 6 seconds.\n4. Repeat at an easy pace without strain.","hidden":false,"enabled":true,"has_children":false,"is_starter":false,"notifications_enabled":false},
{"id":"49eac358-c46e-5ec5-a29a-79b638e1e503","protocol_id":"0c5ca4a7-0e1f-4a52-9a0b-5c1c6c1f0a31","display_name":"Calf Rolling","item_type":"activity","kind":"action","category":"do","subtype":"exercise","group_name":"2. Release (8–10 min)","scheduled_time":"07:07:00","duration_minutes":1,"day_number":10,"sort_order":50,"recurrence_type":"daily","recurrence_interval_unit":"day","catalog_activity_id":"activity_oscar_calf_rolling","notes":"Suggested complete session: a synthesis of lower-risk elements from the catalogue, not an exact routine published by Oscar. Dose: 30 seconds per side.\n1. Sit with one calf on a roller or ball, hands behind you.\n2. Roll from just above the ankle toward just below the knee.\n3. Turn the leg slightly in and out to reach the sides.\n4. Repeat with the other calf.","hidden":false,"enabled":true,"has_children":false,"is_starter":false,"notifications_enabled":false},
{"id":"73b81fc6-b8aa-5042-9478-a7799e8b5639","protocol_id":"0c5ca4a7-0e1f-4a52-9a0b-5c1c6c1f0a31","display_name":"Macebell Spirals","item_type":"activity","kind":"action","category":"do","subtype":"exercise","group_name":"Full-body activation, spirals and twists","scheduled_time":"07:15:00","duration_minutes":5,"day_number":1,"sort_order":50,"recurrence_type":"daily","recurrence_interval_unit":"day","catalog_activity_id":"activity_oscar_macebell_spirals","notes":"Dose: 2–3 sessions per week; no fixed reps.\n1. Begin with an unweighted stick or broom handle to learn the pattern.\n2. Practise slow rotational swings from one shoulder to the other.\n3. Move on to smooth figure-eight patterns once the spirals are easy.\n4. Keep your wrists and shoulders comfortable throughout.\n5. Return to a neutral stance between sequences.","hidden":false,"enabled":true,"has_children":false,"is_starter":false,"notifications_enabled":false},
{"id":"77761a2c-21ef-5213-a2cb-66f8b23201c0","protocol_id":"0c5ca4a7-0e1f-4a52-9a0b-5c1c6c1f0a31","display_name":"Side-neck stretch","item_type":"activity","kind":"action","category":"do","subtype":"exercise","group_name":"Neck training","scheduled_time":"07:15:00","duration_minutes":1,"day_number":6,"sort_order":50,"recurrence_type":"daily","recurrence_interval_unit":"day","catalog_activity_id":"activity_neck_stretch_lateral","notes":"Ear toward shoulder for 15 seconds per side. This is an existing catalog activity; its full steps are on the activity.","hidden":false,"enabled":true,"has_children":false,"is_starter":false,"notifications_enabled":false},
{"id":"c026c528-f8f4-5b9d-b2b1-652e70458c74","protocol_id":"0c5ca4a7-0e1f-4a52-9a0b-5c1c6c1f0a31","display_name":"Comfortable Nasal Breathing","item_type":"activity","kind":"action","category":"do","subtype":"wellness","group_name":"Facial taping and passive practices","scheduled_time":"07:00:00","duration_minutes":2,"day_number":9,"sort_order":50,"recurrence_type":"daily","recurrence_interval_unit":"day","catalog_activity_id":"activity_oscar_comfortable_nasal_breathing","notes":"Dose: Encouraged when the airway is clear.\n1. Make sure your nose is clear and breathing through it feels easy.\n2. Close your lips softly without pressing them together.\n3. Breathe in and out through your nose at an easy pace.\n4. If your nose is blocked or breathing feels hard, return to easy mouth breathing and see a clinician if it keeps happening.","hidden":false,"enabled":true,"has_children":false,"is_starter":false,"notifications_enabled":false},
{"id":"cf17ad15-d310-590d-be7b-660700873135","protocol_id":"0c5ca4a7-0e1f-4a52-9a0b-5c1c6c1f0a31","display_name":"Static Back","item_type":"activity","kind":"action","category":"do","subtype":"exercise","group_name":"Posture, pelvis and spine","scheduled_time":"07:13:00","duration_minutes":5,"day_number":3,"sort_order":50,"recurrence_type":"daily","recurrence_interval_unit":"day","catalog_activity_id":"activity_oscar_static_back","notes":"Dose: Not specified by Oscar; 3–5 minutes is a comfortable start.\n1. Lie on your back.\n2. Rest your lower legs on a chair or bench.\n3. Bend your hips and knees to roughly 90 degrees.\n4. Rest your arms out to the sides, palms up.\n5. Breathe comfortably and let the body relax.","hidden":false,"enabled":true,"has_children":false,"is_starter":false,"notifications_enabled":false},
